# Spec discussion stays in the spec

When the user is discussing, drafting, reviewing, or amending a spec, make no application code changes. That work is read-only. The only files you may edit are inside `specs/`.

Not allowed until they explicitly ask to implement:

- `apps/**`, tests, generated data, content JSON, config, lockfiles, or any other application code

```text
User: "On the spec, a quiz with 2 of 4 answered should reopen on the third."
❌ QuizGame.tsx, progress helpers, or a drive-by fix
✅ specs/026-quiz-resume.md (and the 000 / README status lines if the child is registered)

User: "Implement 026."
✅ Code changes for that spec are in scope.
```

Do not treat writing or updating a spec as permission to start the implementation.
